# Secure Coding Instructions
Always write secure code from the start. Never defer security fixes.
- Before coding, read SKILL.md and templates/<language>.md.
- Before writing a route, auth, data model, upload, outbound call or LLM tool,
  ask the five security frontiers in checks/secure-grilling.md with your
  recommended secure default for each. Do not guess these silently.
- When handling LLM tools or RAG, review checks/llm-top10.md.
- After writing code, run `node hooks/scan.js --staged` and fix any reported findings immediately.
- Before declaring done, run `node hooks/gate.js --check`. It exits 2 until you
  answer ownership, authorization, taint and failure-direction — the checks no
  pattern can see. Name the check or answer "N/A".
